        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;What gets deployed (script: azure-virtualwan-inter-region-azfw.sh, RG lab-vwan-irazfw-4)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 1 Standard vWAN, 2 Standard vHubs, 2 hub VPN gateways; 2 branch VNets with VpnGw1Az gateways; 2 BGP VPN site connections, each with a local gateway and a branch-side connection&lt;br&gt;• 10 VNets (branch1/2, spoke1-8) and 8 Ubuntu 22.04 VMs (branch1VM, branch2VM, spoke1/3/5/6/7/8VM) with 8 Standard public IPs, plus 2 VPN gateway public IPs&lt;br&gt;• 2 Azure Firewalls (spoke2-azfw, spoke4-azfw) with 4 public IPs, 2 firewall policies (Any-to-Any allow) and 2 Log Analytics workspaces with diagnostics&lt;br&gt;• 8 VNet peerings (spoke2 to 5/6, spoke4 to 7/8); 2 route tables (default route to firewall) on spoke5-8; 2 NSGs (SSH only from the deploying machine's public IP) on each main subnet&lt;br&gt;• spoke1/spoke3 connect to their hubs normally; spoke2/spoke4 connect with a static route to their firewall; hub default route tables forward 10.2.0.0/16 and 10.4.0.0/16 to spoke2conn/spoke4conn&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Legend:&lt;/b&gt; blue = vHub connection/hub link, orange dashed = S2S VPN with BGP, purple thick = VNet peering, red = Azure Firewall, yellow = branch, purple = spoke" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="825" width="1560" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
